# A Structure of a callable's own data is visible to its code by reference (plan M11 5b; R20: one instance, the graph
# of the part data, shared by every call): the code finds Point in the registry of the launch's data, with no row. The
# Structure is written in one line: a block closed by `end:` inside the parentheses of the part data is a later step
# of 5b.
fn: f () int (
    Point(int: x 4)
)
    return: Point\x
end: f
int: seen f()
